      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today, we’re announcing the Web Search API on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Simpler integration for existing applications – Applications that already have their own API layer can call the Web Search API directly, adding web grounding without adopting the full AgentCore Gateway stack.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The Web Search API is the InvokeWebSearch operation on the bedrock-agentcore data plane, the same endpoint that other AgentCore tools such as AgentCore Browser , a capability of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, use.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: How a Web Search API request flows",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If your code runs on AWS Lambda , Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) , Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2) , or Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) , the execution role provides credentials automatically.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Without a framework, the WebSearchClient in the AgentCore Python SDK wraps the same call and returns results with parsed dates. langchain-aws 1.9.3 and the AgentCore Python SDK 1.26.0 add Web Search API support, so install those versions or later.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T18:15:09.746Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can try the Web Search API in the Amazon Bedrock AgentCore console before you write any code.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/introducing-the-web-search-api-on-amazon-bedrock-agentcore/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:13:16.000Z",
